### ============================================================
### X MCP Client — Spring AI 2.0
### ============================================================
###
### This HTTP file demonstrates the two REST endpoints exposed by
### the application.
###
### 1. /docs
###    Uses the X Documentation MCP server:
###    https://docs.x.com/mcp
###
###    Claude can discover and invoke the documentation tools
###    exposed by the remote MCP server.
###
###    No X Bearer Token is required.
###
### 2. /search
###    Uses the live X API MCP server:
###    https://api.x.com/mcp
###
###    Claude can discover and invoke X API tools to search recent
###    posts. This requires X_BEARER_TOKEN to be configured.
###
### ============================================================


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Demo 1 — Query the X API Documentation
### ------------------------------------------------------------
###
### Endpoint:
###   GET /docs
###
### What happens under the hood:
###
###   HTTP Client
###       |
###       v
###   Spring Boot /docs
###       |
###       v
###   ChatClient
###       |
###       v
###   Claude
###       |
###       | AI decides a tool is needed
###       v
###   X Docs MCP Server
###       |
###       v
###   Documentation Search Tool
###       |
###       v
###   Claude generates the final answer
###
### The question is defined inside DocsController.
### Claude uses the tools exposed by the `x-docs` MCP connection
### to find the relevant X API documentation.
###
### No authentication is required for the X documentation server.

GET http://localhost:8080/docs
Accept: text/plain


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Demo 2 — Search Recent X Posts
### ------------------------------------------------------------
###
### Endpoint:
###   GET /search?topic=<topic>
###
### The `topic` parameter is optional.
###
### If omitted, the controller uses:
###
###   Spring Boot 4.1
###
### The request is passed to Claude, which decides which tools
### exposed by the `x-api` MCP server should be invoked.
###
### Authentication flow:
###
###   X_BEARER_TOKEN
###          |
###          v
###   XApiAuthConfig
###          |
###          | Authorization: Bearer <token>
###          v
###   https://api.x.com/mcp
###
### The bearer token is added only to requests targeting
### `api.x.com`.
###
### IMPORTANT:
### Never put the actual X bearer token in this HTTP file.
### Configure it as an environment variable instead.
###

GET http://localhost:8080/search?topic=Spring%20AI
Accept: text/plain


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Demo 2 — Search Another Topic
### ------------------------------------------------------------
###
### The endpoint accepts any topic.
###
### Example:
###   Spring Boot
###   Java 21
###   MCP
###   AI Agents
###   Kafka
###   Kubernetes
###
### Claude will formulate the MCP tool call based on the
### user's requested topic.

GET http://localhost:8080/search?topic=AI%20Agents
Accept: text/plain


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Demo 2 — Search for MCP Discussions
### ------------------------------------------------------------

GET http://localhost:8080/search?topic=MCP
Accept: text/plain


### ============================================================
### Expected Architecture
### ============================================================
###
###                    Spring Boot 4.1
###                          |
###                     ChatClient
###                          |
###                       Claude
###                    /           \
###                   /             \
###                  v               v
###           X Docs MCP       X API MCP
###             Server            Server
###                |                 |
###          Documentation       Live X API
###             Tools              Tools
###
### Claude receives BOTH MCP tool sets through the shared
### ToolCallbackProvider configured in ChatClientConfig.
###
### The model decides which tools to invoke based on the request.
###
### ============================================================